<<tag character:Narrator>>
<<tag lore_id:lore_inn_painting>>
Narrator: A painting hangs crooked above the hearth, varnish gone amber with smoke and decades.
Narrator: Echohaven in its prime — copper-domed, glass-throated, the river running silver under three white bridges.
Narrator: No mud. No pit. The cathedral spire pierces a sky the colour of struck flint.
Narrator: A faded brass plate reads: "Echohaven, the year before the silence."
Narrator: Someone — Bob, perhaps — has tucked a sprig of dried heather behind the frame. A small act of remembering.
===
